  "term": "Horner’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Horner’s syndrome is a condition caused by impaired sympathetic nerve supply to one side of the face, including the eye. It is marked by a small pupil, slight drooping of the upper eyelid, and reduced sweating on the affected side of the face.",
